    /**
     * Spreads a draft over the number of monthly instalments at the annual interest rate, after a down
     * payment of the percentage of the grand total; empty if no
     * such invoice. Both have already been checked; any invoice that is not a draft, a credit note, or
     * one holding back retention is refused, as is a plan whose monthly instalment would be worth less
     * than {@link Invoice#MIN_INSTALMENT_USD} US dollars at today's rates.
     */
    @Transactional
    public Optional<Invoice> setPlan(Long invoiceId, int instalments, BigDecimal instalmentRate,
            BigDecimal planDownPct) {
        Optional<Invoice> found = load(invoiceId);
        found.ifPresent(invoice -> {
            if (invoice.isCreditNote()) {
                throw new InvoiceRejectedException("A credit note cannot be spread over instalments.");
            }
            if (!invoice.isDraft()) {
                throw new InvoiceRejectedException("Only a draft can be spread over instalments.");
            }
            if (invoice.getRetentionPct().signum() > 0) {
                throw new InvoiceRejectedException("An invoice holding back retention cannot also be spread over instalments.");
            }
            invoice.setPlan(instalments, instalmentRate, planDownPct);
            if (invoice.isInstalmentTooSmall(taxRate.percent(), today.date())) {
                throw new InvoiceRejectedException("The monthly instalment must be worth at least $"
                        + Invoice.MIN_INSTALMENT_USD.toPlainString() + " at today's exchange rates.");
            }
            invoices.saveAndFlush(invoice);
        });
        return found;
    }

    /**
     * Releases the given amount of the retention held back on a sent invoice today (all that is still
     * held when it is null), adding it to the amount due (all that is released falling due
     * {@link Invoice#RETENTION_DUE_DAYS} days after the latest release), and records the amount
     * released in the audit; empty if no such invoice. Refused while anything other than retention
     * already released is still due, when there is no retention held to release, or when the amount is
     * more than is held.
     */
    @Transactional
    public Optional<Invoice> releaseRetention(Long invoiceId, BigDecimal amount) {
     * {@code retentionPct} (without trailing zeros) is the share of the amount before tax (subtotal less discount) held back as
     * {@code retention}, rounded down to the cent and never more than {@code retentionCap} (null for no cap); {@code retentionHeld} is what is still held back (not
     * part of the amount due), {@code retentionReleasedOn} the day of the latest release (null while none is released) and
     * {@code retentionDueDate} the day all that is released falls due. {@code instalments} is how many
     * monthly instalments it is spread over (null without a plan) at the annual {@code instalmentRate}
     * (without trailing zeros), after a down payment of {@code planDownPct} percent of the grand total
     * (without trailing zeros; instalment 0 when not 0); {@code schedule} lists them and {@code planTotal} is what they add up to
     * (null without a plan), from which what is paid comes off for the amount due. {@code listedDueDate}
     * is the due date as listed: for a plan, its next unpaid instalment's. {@code currency} is the
     * currency its client is billed in, which every amount is in (whole yen for a yen client).
     * {@code earlyDiscount} is the early-payment discount it was settled with (0 when none), and
     * {@code settleAmount} what would settle it today while its early-payment window is open (null otherwise).
     * {@code lateInterest} is the late interest charged on it so far, part of the amount due;
     * {@code lateWaived} is the late interest written off by waiving it (0 when none was). {@code payoff} is what would pay off its
     * plan today (null without a plan or once it is paid off), and {@code interestSaved} the interest
     * of instalments not yet due that paying it off early dropped (0 when none was). {@code fxDifference}
     * is, for a client billed in another currency, the exchange difference in US dollars of the payments
     * applied to it (see {@link Invoice#fxDifference(List)}); null for a dollar invoice.
     * {@code writtenOffOn} is the day it was written off as a bad debt (null when it was not); everything
     * it still owed then is in {@code writtenOff}, and nothing is due. {@code net} is the amount before tax; when
     * {@code pricesIncludeTax} the tax is inside the subtotal less the discount, which is then the grand total.
     * {@code cashDue} is the amount due rounded down to the cash coin below (0.05, or whole yen) and
     * {@code cashRounding} the difference (signed): once settled in cash, the cash rounding it was settled with.
     * {@code surchargePct} (without trailing zeros) is the rush surcharge percentage and {@code surcharge} that share of
     * the subtotal less the discount, rounded down to the cent; it counts towards the {@code minimumCharge}.
     * {@code withholding} is what the client withholds for its tax office (0 when none): never owed, so
     * left out of the amount due; nothing when reverse charged. {@code withholdingPct} (without trailing zeros)
     * is the client's withholding percentage.
